  "question": {
    "text": "A radar has a power of $1 \\mathrm{~Kw}$ and is operating at a frequency of $10 \\mathrm{~GHz}$. It is located on a mountain top of height $500 \\mathrm{~m}$. The maximum distance upto which it can detect object located on the surface of the earth (Radius of earth $=6.4 \\times 10^6 \\mathrm{~m}$ ) is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "cqB5f",
      "text": "\n$80 \\mathrm{~km}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "vxWEo",
      "text": "\n$16 \\mathrm{~km}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2h96l",
      "text": "\n$40 \\mathrm{~km}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Ievbd",
      "text": "\n$64 \\mathrm{~km}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Maximum distance on earth where object can be detected is $\\mathrm{d}$, then\n$\\begin{array}{ll} \n& (h+R)^2=d^2+R^2 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & d^2=h^2+2 R h \\\\\n\\text { since } & h < < R, \\quad \\Rightarrow d^2=2 h R \\\\\n\\Rightarrow & d=\\sqrt{2(500)\\left(6.4 \\times 10^6\\right)}=80 \\mathrm{~km}\n\\end{array}$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/CJx5bNuxeOmXeKmpIErUaSzeDcpis2chmoM5uUIZpU0.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
